{%- comment -%}
  Enforces the subscription bag minimum in the cart.

  The 18% subscription discount rides on the selling plan attached to a cart line, and
  Shopify treats quantity and selling plan as independent. So the minimum enforced by the
  PDP buy box has no authority once a line exists: reducing a line's quantity, or removing
  one line of a multi-line subscription, leaves the remaining lines discounted below the
  minimum. Both routes were reachable from the cart drawer.

  The rule is on the TOTAL across every subscription line, not per line, because
  2 Smooth Talker + 1 Blueprint is a legitimate three bags spread over two lines.

  When the total is short this shows a notice, blocks checkout, and offers the two ways out:
  top the subscription back up, or drop to one-time pricing and keep shopping.

  Not a substitute for server-side validation. A crafted cart permalink still reaches
  Shopify's checkout directly. A cart validation function is the airtight version and is
  the intended follow-up; this covers every route a real shopper has.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- render 'vite-tag', entry: 'sections/styles/heist-subscription-minimum.scss' -%}
{%- render 'vite-tag', entry: 'sections/scripts/heist-subscription-minimum.js' -%}

<div class="heist-sub-min" data-heist-sub-min data-min-bags="3" hidden>
  <p class="heist-sub-min__text t-n1" data-sub-min-text></p>
  <div class="heist-sub-min__actions">
    <button type="button" class="heist-sub-min__btn" data-sub-min-add></button>
    <button type="button" class="heist-sub-min__btn heist-sub-min__btn--ghost" data-sub-min-onetime>
      Switch to one-time
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
